Path: deploy/ppocr-android/ppocr-sdk

Vendored at commit 211989f046cc1878460f9e65574690c00a127a1a (2026-06-26) into
vendor/ppocr-sdk/src/main: a straight copy of the non-UI OCR pipeline (ONNX Runtime session
management, detection/recognition preprocessing, DB postprocessing (NMS/box-sort), perspective crop,
CTC decode). The pristine upstream source is kept as a git submodule at vendor/paddleocr-upstream,
sparse-checked-out to just deploy/ppocr-android/ppocr-sdk (PaddleOCR itself is a large monorepo we
otherwise have no use for).

Local patch 1 of 2: load models from raw bytes/files, not just APK assets. Upstream's
`ORTSessionManager`/`ModelConfig`/`OCREngine`/`PaddleOCR` only ever read model/config files from
`context.assets`, but Vision's models are downloaded at runtime into app-internal storage (never
bundled in the APK or committed to git — see vox-vision/src/main/java/com/voxapps/vision/ocr/). Added
purely-additive overloads (`ORTSessionManager.loadModels(ByteArray, ByteArray)`,
`ModelConfig.parse(String, String)`, `OCREngine`'s `detModelBytes`/`recModelBytes`/`recConfigContent`
constructor params, `PaddleOCR.create(..., detModelFile: File, recModelFile: File, recConfigFile:
File)`) — every original asset-path-based method/constructor is untouched and still works.

Local patch 2 of 2: the OpenCV 5 geometry API. Upstream targets OpenCV 4.x, where `minAreaRect` and
`getPerspectiveTransform` live on `Imgproc`; we build OpenCV 5.0, which moved both into
`org.opencv.geometry.Geometry`. `DBPostProcessor` and `QuadTextCrop` are rewritten to call them
there. The failure this prevents is deceptive: with `Imgproc.minAreaRect` unresolved, the
`RotatedRect` it returns has no type either, so `.size` and `.points` fail too and one missing symbol
reads as a dozen unrelated errors in files nobody touched.

Both patches are maintained as real, storable diffs under patches/ (regenerate with
scripts/regen_ppocr_sdk_patch.sh whenever a patch changes). Which files belong to which patch is read
out of the patch itself, so adding one to that folder is the whole of adding a patch — nothing else
lists them. scripts/check_ppocr_sdk_version.sh checks whether upstream has moved past the pinned
commit and whether each stored patch would still apply cleanly against the newer tree.

Used by vox-vision for on-device OCR (PP-OCRv5 mobile detection + recognition models). Model files
themselves are NOT vendored here — they are downloaded at runtime from a GitHub Release on this repo
(tag ocr-models-v1) into app-internal storage, mirroring how vox-commander already handles
Whisper/Vosk models. See vox-vision/src/main/java/com/voxapps/vision/ocr/ for the download +
integration code.

